spection equipment support and visual-method environment: non-designated lamp spectral shift.\",\"safeIndependentContinuation\":\"Install the designated neutral spare, verify the white reference tile and retained approved cloth, and repeat non-destructive visual comparisons for each lot against the in-band reflectance results.\",\"retainedEvidenceSufficient\":true,\"repeatedLoopDetected\":false,\"smallestAdvancingAction\":\"Replace the main-table lamp with the available designated spare and repeat the prescribed non-destructive visual comparisons.\",\"authorityClass\":\"NO_NEW_AUTHORITY\",\"authorizationBasis\":\"Current authority expressly permits replacing inspection lamps with designated spares and repeating non-destructive visual comparisons; E05 confirms the spare is available and installable by the inspection lead.\",\"prohibitedOperations\":[\"Redye accepted cloth without product evidence.\",\"Change the reflectance acceptance band.\"],\"uncertainties\":[\"Final lot acceptance outcomes remain pending until comparisons are repeated under the designated neutral lamp.\"],\"boundedRationaleSummary\":\"In-band strips, location-dependent appearance, reference-tile shift, and identical distortion of retained approved cloth positively localize the defect to the replacement lamp. The available designated spare provides a contained, already-authorized resolution path.\"}"
